WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:02.400
To become psychologically flexible

00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:04.800
is more than just
addressing personality.

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:08.640
It's actually addressing the way
we really relate to ourselves.

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:13.880
Flexibility is the ability to adjust
your thoughts, actions and feelings

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:16.440
to the circumstances
you find yourself in.

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:20.200
Situations change,
and so it's important to be able

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:24.520
to adjust and behave in the most
functional way to achieve your goals.

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:33.920
When you're born,
your brain is not finished.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.040
Infant brains are born
under construction.

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:39.720
They're waiting for a set
of wiring instructions

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:40.880
from the world.

00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:45.320
If you expose your children
to a lot of varying experiences

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:47.600
then you're basically wiring
your child's brain

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:49.600
to function in a flexible way

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:52.200
and to learn new things
when necessary.

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:55.880
If your child's experiences
are very restricted

00:00:56.480 --> 00:00:59.880
then your child will have less
flexibility to adjust their actions

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:01.880
to the situations that they're in.

00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:05.040
There's a really well-known

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:06.680
demonstration of flexibility

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:08.080
called the Stroop test.

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:12.160
A sequence of words,
such as red, green, yellow, blue

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:13.800
but written in different colours.

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:17.600
When you present people
with a whole list of these

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:21.160
you find that it takes people longer
to name the colour of the ink

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:24.840
when the word is written in a colour
that is different to the actual word.

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:26.800
The idea behind that

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:28.440
is in order to be able
to name the colour

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:30.120
requires people
to switch between

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:32.440
different pieces of information
in their mind.

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:34.040
In simple terms,

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:36.960
what happens is that
when they scan the word colour

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:39.720
the automatic processes
of reading the word

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:43.280
interfere with the person's ability
to state the colour out loud.

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:46.360
The more difficult
people find this generally

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:48.400
the less cognitively flexible
they are.

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:52.960
When your brain
can't predict something,

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:57.200
or when you have to take in new
information that you didn't predict,

00:01:57.280 --> 00:01:59.840
that's what we call learning.

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:03.120
So your brain can update,
it can learn,

00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:06.960
or your brain can ignore
the sense data

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:08.840
and just go with its own prediction.

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:15.400
Flexibility means tailoring
a response to the specific situation,

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:17.320
either by predicting well

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:20.440
or by learning when
there is prediction error.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:24.840
A lot of what psychological
flexibility is about

00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:27.480
is the way in which people use
resources that they have available

00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:29.240
in dealing with stress.

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:32.440
One of the things about
psychological inflexibility

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:34.640
is that people are not
using their resources

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:36.160
in a way that's helpful to them.

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:39.160
Quite often they're using a very
narrow range of their resources

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:40.840
to be able to adapt.

00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:42.520
And the idea

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:44.520
in psychological flexibility

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:46.040
is really to move people

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:49.800
from a state of what psychologists
call languishing,

00:02:49.880 --> 00:02:53.000
of being stuck in a less than
satisfactory situation,

00:02:53.080 --> 00:02:54.760
to move them out of that zone

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:57.640
into a zone of achieving
more of their potential.

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:00.200
What stops people
from changing their lives

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:03.600
from a state of low satisfaction
to one of higher satisfaction

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:06.240
is quite often to do
with inflexibility

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:08.880
in the way they approach
the problem that they're facing.

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:14.040
So there's a really deep lesson here.

00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:15.920
You can take more control

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:17.840
over your environment.

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:22.280
You are not just a passive recipient
of whatever the world gives you.

00:03:24.520 --> 00:03:28.080
Spending time cultivating experiences

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:30.560
and foraging for new information

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:34.880
is an investment in maintaining
a flexible brain.

00:03:35.720 --> 00:03:40.600
These are all opportunities to expose
yourself to prediction error

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:44.360
so that your brain can solve problems
more flexibly in the future.

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:48.640
So exposing yourself
to stuff you don't know,

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:51.560
and maybe even ideas you don't like,

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:55.200
might make you feel crappy
in the moment

00:03:55.280 --> 00:03:57.680
but actually

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:01.640
it is a really good investment.

